 Water Filter Guide: Which Filter Fits Your Model? A simple guide to Samsung refrigerator water filters: part numbers, how to find yours, how to replace it and how to reset the filter light.", "Guide"], ["LG refrigerator water filters: which one do you need?", "/guides/lg-refrigerator-water-filter-guide/", "LG Refrigerator Water Filter Guide: Which Filter Fits Your Model? A simple guide to LG refrigerator water filters: part numbers, how to find yours, how to replace it and how to reset the filter light.", "Guide"], ["Whirlpool refrigerator water filters: which one do you need?", "/guides/whirlpool-refrigerator-water-filter-guide/", "Whirlpool Refrigerator Water Filter Guide: Which Filter Fits Your Model? A simple guide to Whirlpool refrigerator water filters: part numbers, how to find yours, how to replace it and how to reset the filter light.", "Guide"], ["GE refrigerator water filters: which one do you need?", "/guides/ge-refrigerator-water-filter-guide/", "GE Refrigerator Water Filter Guide: Which Filter Fits Your Model? A simple guide to GE refrigerator water filters: part numbers, how to find yours, how to replace it and how to reset the filter light.", "Guide"], ["Refrigerator water tastes bad after changing the filter", "/guides/refrigerator-water-tastes-bad-after-changing-the-filter/", "Refrigerator Water Tastes Bad After Changing the Filter? Causes and Fixes If your fridge water tastes or smells odd after a filter change, the cause is usually trapped air, carbon dust or old ice. Here is what to try.", "Guide"], ["What to do when a refrigerator water filter is stuck", "/guides/refrigerator-water-filter-wont-twist-off/", "Refrigerator Water Filter Stuck? How to Remove It Without Breaking It A stuck refrigerator water filter is common. Try these safe tips to loosen it and what to avoid.", "Guide"], ["Why is my refrigerator water dispenser slow?", "/guides/refrigerator-water-dispenser-slow-or-low-flow/", "Refrigerator Water Dispenser Slow? Low Water Flow Causes If your refrigerator water dispenser is slow or the flow is weak, a clogged filter is the most common cause. Here is how to check.", "Guide"], ["Refrigerator water filter leaking: what to check", "/guides/refrigerator-water-filter-leaking/", "Refrigerator Water Filter Leaking? Common Causes and Fixes A leaking refrigerator water filter is usually not seated, has a damaged O-ring or is the wrong part. Here is how to troubleshoot it.", "Guide"], ["Do you need a refrigerator water filter?", "/guides/do-you-need-a-refrigerator-water-filter/", "Do You Need a Refrigerator Water Filter? Can You Use a Bypass Plug? Is a refrigerator water filter necessary? What it does, what a bypass plug is and when to replace the filter.", "Guide"], ["Internal vs external refrigerator water filters", "/guides/internal-vs-external-refrigerator-water-filters/", "Internal vs External Refrigerator Water Filters: Which Is Better? Internal cartridges vs external inline filters for refrigerators: differences, installation and when to choose each.", "Guide"], ["What do NSF/ANSI 42, 53 and 401 mean?", "/guides/what-do-nsf-ansi-42-53-and-401-mean/", "What Do NSF/ANSI 42, 53 and 401 Mean on a Refrigerator Water Filter? A plain-English explanation of the NSF/ANSI standards you see on refrigerator water filter packaging.", "Guide"], ["How to tell which refrigerator water filter fits", "/guides/how-to-tell-which-refrigerator-water-filter-fits/", "How to Tell Which Refrigerator Water Filter Fits Your Fridge Four ways to find the right refrigerator water filter: model number, old filter part number, shape and the owner's manual.", "Guide"], ["Water filter light stays on after changing the filter", "/guides/water-filter-light-stays-on-after-changing-filter/", "Refrigerator Water Filter Light Stays On After Changing the Filter The filter light is still on even though you changed the filter? Check that you reset it, that the filter is locked and what else to try.", "Guide"], ["Cloudy ice or smelly ice from